From b44b335ba0e161f84eead9485e39b870e309a222 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 14:22:19 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/5] feat(ui): viewport Display menu with four display modes,
 Look at and graphics switches

The viewport toolbar gets a Display button. Its menu has three groups:
the display mode (Shaded, with edges / Shaded / Wireframe / Shaded, with
hidden edges), Look at a face, and Graphics (grid, origin axes,
projection). Each entry is view state and queues no command.

- draw_list::plan gives the pass order of each display mode from the
  cached index partition; View3D::render_with follows it.
- "Shaded, with hidden edges" draws the cached model edges a second time
  with the depth test reversed, blended thin.
- Look at arms one click and turns the view to the normal of the face
  under the cursor (Camera::toward). It selects nothing.
- The display mode and the grid switch are kept in view.json with the
  gizmo names. An old file loads the defaults.
- The display mode choice moved out of the Browser pane.

Ground shadow, ambient occlusion and the quality preset are not in this
change; a follow-up issue has them.

Fixes #2818

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
