From 179ef8a3f44c9b1a1b93c3491e121edd81d23f5d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 01:50:53 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] feat(ui): "Wireframe, see-through" display mode

The Display menu has a fifth display mode. It draws each edge of the
model and of the stock, front and back, and no face: not to the color
buffer and not to the depth buffer. The model hides nothing behind it.

A click in the mode picks hidden edges too, by the existing rule of
`pick_bodies`: nearest to the cursor first, then nearest to the camera.
The toolbar's wireframe switch treats the mode as a wireframe. The view
file stores the mode as `wireframe-see-through`.

Stacked on #2835 (#2818), which adds "Shaded" without edges, the draw
list and the saved display mode.

Fixes #2636

